(3) a corrections staff person working in a public agency and supervising offenders in the community as defined in sections 243.05, subdivision 6; 244.19, subdivision 1; and 401.01, subdivision 2;
(4) [-an individual employed on a full-time basis by the state or by a fire department of a governmental subdivision of the state-][+ a full-time firefighter or part-time firefighter working for the state or for a fire department of a governmental subdivision of the state or a volunteer firefighter or paid on-call firefighter working for a fire department of a governmental subdivision of the state or an independent nonprofit firefighting corporation+], who is engaged in any of the following duties:
